content:
A PNG extension does not tell you whether an image contains useful transparency. A fully opaque PNG can look correct on white and show a rectangle on a colored page. Inspect the alpha channel and composite the image on several backgrounds before accepting a cutout.

## Separate format, transparency and visual quality

PNG can represent transparency, while JPEG does not preserve an alpha channel. Transparent pixels and good subject edges are separate questions: an image can contain transparent pixels and still have halos, clipped details or an unwanted shadow. Keep a source copy, export a PNG when alpha is required and inspect the exact file that will be delivered.

A checkerboard is an editor convention, not proof that the file is transparent. Sometimes a checkerboard is itself part of the image. A pixel inspection or a compositing test distinguishes these cases.

## Inspect a local file in a browser

This example takes a user-selected local file and reports fully transparent, partially transparent and opaque pixels. Put these elements in an HTML file and load the JavaScript as a module. The 4 MiB and 8-million-pixel limits are demonstration choices. Decode allocation happens before the dimension check, so this is an inspection tool, not a hardened upload service.

```html
<label for="cutout">Choose a PNG to inspect</label>
<input id="cutout" type="file" accept="image/png">
<p id="alpha-result" role="status"></p>
<canvas id="preview" aria-label="Selected image preview"></canvas>
```

```javascript
const input = document.querySelector('#cutout');
const output = document.querySelector('#alpha-result');
const canvas = document.querySelector('#preview');
let revision = 0;

input.addEventListener('change', async () => {
  const current = ++revision;
  const file = input.files?.[0];
  if (!file || file.size > 4 * 1024 * 1024) {
    output.textContent = 'Choose a PNG no larger than 4 MiB.';
    return;
  }
  let bitmap;
  try {
    bitmap = await createImageBitmap(file);
    if (current !== revision) return;
    if (bitmap.width * bitmap.height > 8_000_000) throw new Error('Too large');
    canvas.width = bitmap.width;
    canvas.height = bitmap.height;
    const context = canvas.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true });
    if (!context) throw new Error('Canvas unavailable');
    context.drawImage(bitmap, 0, 0);
    const { data } = context.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
    const counts = { transparent: 0, partial: 0, opaque: 0 };
    for (let i = 3; i < data.length; i += 4) {
      if (data[i] === 0) counts.transparent++;
      else if (data[i] === 255) counts.opaque++;
      else counts.partial++;
    }
    output.textContent = `Transparent: ${counts.transparent}; partial: ${counts.partial}; opaque: ${counts.opaque}`;
  } catch {
    if (current === revision) output.textContent = 'Unable to inspect this image.';
  } finally {
    bitmap?.close();
  }
});
```

This counts the decoded canvas representation. It does not inspect original PNG chunk encoding or certify edge quality. A cross-origin remote image can make a canvas unreadable without appropriate CORS permission; selecting a local file avoids that remote-image case. Do not work around origin restrictions.

## Look at the boundary, not only the counts

Composite the image on white, near-black and a saturated color at the intended display size. Inspect hair, reflective surfaces, holes and soft shadows. Partially transparent edge pixels are often expected from antialiasing; removing them indiscriminately can create jagged edges. A white fringe may come from color contamination in edge pixels and needs a visual correction rather than a lower file-size target.

If you create a cutout with [RemovePhotoBG](https://removephotobg.com/), inspect its exported PNG using this same process. Keep the final alpha-capable asset through later resizing and delivery. An accidental JPEG conversion will flatten the image even if the original was transparent.

## Keep reproducible fixtures

Use a fully opaque PNG, a PNG with a transparent hole, a soft-edge PNG and an image containing a painted checkerboard. Record expected counts for small synthetic fixtures; use visual review for real edges. Recheck the final downloaded asset after any optimization step. [Upload validation](../validating-image-uploads-in-javascript/) handles acceptance, while the [secure pipeline guide](../building-a-secure-image-processing-pipeline/) covers isolation and output promotion.

